1
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:15,810
Welcome, Lord Stark.

2
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:19,220
Grand Maester Pycelle has called a meeting of the small council.

3
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:21,300
The honor of your presence is requested.

4
00:02:23,050 --> 00:02:26,110
Get the girls settled in. I'll be back in time for supper.

5
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:28,770
- And, Jory, you go with them. - Yes, my Lord.

6
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:32,410
If you'd like to change into something more appropriate...

7
00:03:08,750 --> 00:03:10,980
Thank the gods you're here, Stark.

8
00:03:11,780 --> 00:03:15,240
About time we had some stern northern leadership.

9
00:03:15,910 --> 00:03:18,100
Glad to see you're protecting the throne.

10
00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:19,890
Sturdy old thing.

11
00:03:20,050 --> 00:03:22,320
How many kings' asses have polished it, I wonder?

12
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:24,210
Um, what's the line?

13
00:03:24,420 --> 00:03:28,050
The king shits and the Hand wipes.

14
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:30,360
Very handsome armor.

15
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:33,520
- Not a scratch on it. - I know.

16
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,800
People have been swinging at me for years,

17
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,520
but they always seem to miss.

18
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:40,230
You've chosen your opponents wisely then.

19
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:42,890
I have a knack for it.

20
00:03:46,390 --> 00:03:49,880
It must be strange for you coming into this room.

21
00:03:51,790 --> 00:03:55,400
I was standing right here when it happened.

22
00:03:55,990 --> 00:03:57,690
He was very brave, your brother.

23
00:03:57,690 --> 00:03:59,570
Your father too.

24
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:02,080
They didn't deserve to die like that.

25
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:04,870
Nobody deserves to die like that.

26
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:06,950
But you just stood there and watched.

27
00:04:07,010 --> 00:04:10,340
500 men just stood there and watched.

28
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:12,670
All the great knights of the Seven Kingdoms...

29
00:04:12,670 --> 00:04:15,550
You think anyone said a word, lifted a finger?

30
00:04:15,950 --> 00:04:17,830
No, Lord Stark.

31
00:04:18,210 --> 00:04:22,560
500 men and this room was silent as a crypt.

32
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:26,660
Except for the screams, of course,

33
00:04:27,290 --> 00:04:29,450
and the Mad King laughing.

34
00:04:29,510 --> 00:04:32,250
And later...

35
00:04:32,310 --> 00:04:34,410
when I watched the Mad King die,

36
00:04:34,580 --> 00:04:38,090
I remembered him laughing as your father burned...

37
00:04:39,390 --> 00:04:41,710
It felt like justice.

38
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:46,560
Is that what you tell yourself at night?

39
00:04:47,690 --> 00:04:50,420
You're a servant of justice?

40
00:04:50,490 --> 00:04:52,120
That you were avenging my father when you

41
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:55,090
shoved your sword in Aerys Targaryen's back?

42
00:04:55,150 --> 00:04:56,950
Tell me...

43
00:04:57,020 --> 00:04:59,950
If I'd stabbed the Mad King in the belly instead of the back,

44
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:02,550
would you admire me more?

45
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:04,970
You served him well

46
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,750
when serving was safe.

47
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:21,870
Lord Stark.

48
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:25,940
Lord Varys.

49
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,790
I was grievously sorry to hear of your

50
00:05:28,790 --> 00:05:29,940
troubles on the Kingsroad.

51
00:05:30,110 --> 00:05:33,550
We are all praying for Prince Joffrey's full recovery.

52
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:36,000
A shame you didn't say a prayer for the butcher's son.

53
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:41,380
Renly! You're looking well.

54
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,250
And you look tired from the road.

55
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:45,520
I told them this meeting could wait another day, but...

56
00:05:45,590 --> 00:05:47,840
But we have a kingdom to look after.

57
00:05:49,290 --> 00:05:51,590
I've hoped to meet you for some time, Lord Stark.

58
00:05:51,650 --> 00:05:53,770
No doubt lady Catelyn has mentioned me.

59
00:05:53,950 --> 00:05:55,530
She has, Lord Baelish.

60
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:58,530
I understand you knew my brother Brandon as well.

61
00:05:58,530 --> 00:06:01,790
All too well. I still carry a token of his esteem

62
00:06:01,790 --> 00:06:03,550
from navel to collarbone.

63
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:05,520
Perhaps you chose the wrong man to duel with.

64
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:07,620
It wasn't the man that I chose, my Lord.

65
00:06:07,690 --> 00:06:09,730
It was Catelyn Tully.

66
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:13,190
A woman worth fighting for, I'm sure you'll agree.

67
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:16,620
I humbly beg your pardon, my Lord Stark.

68
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:18,560
Grand Maester.

69
00:06:19,070 --> 00:06:23,510
How many years has it been? You were a young man.

70
00:06:23,510 --> 00:06:25,070
And you served another king.

71
00:06:26,550 --> 00:06:28,620
Oh, how forgetful of me.

72
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:33,760
This belongs to you, now.

73
00:06:35,890 --> 00:06:37,580
Should we begin?

74
00:06:38,790 --> 00:06:40,620
- Without the king? - Winter may be coming,

75
00:06:40,690 --> 00:06:43,240
but I'm afraid the same cannot be said for my brother.

76
00:06:44,050 --> 00:06:46,050
His grace has many cares.

77
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:49,090
He entrusts some small matters to us

78
00:06:49,150 --> 00:06:50,920
that we might lighten the load.

79
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:53,590
We are the lords of small matters here.

80
00:06:59,410 --> 00:07:01,320
My brother instructs us to stage a tournament

81
00:07:01,390 --> 00:07:04,250
in honor of Lord Stark's appointment as Hand of the King.

82
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:07,890
- Mmm, how much? - 40,000 gold dragons to the champion,

83
00:07:07,950 --> 00:07:09,620
20,000 to the runner-up,

84
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:12,790
20,000 to the winning archer.

85
00:07:12,850 --> 00:07:15,150
Can the treasury bear such expense?

86
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:18,120
I'll have to borrow it. The Lannisters will accommodate, I expect.

87
00:07:18,190 --> 00:07:20,280
We already owe lord Tywin three million gold.

88
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:21,540
What's another 80,000?

89
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:23,750
Are you telling me the Crown is three million in debt?

90
00:07:23,750 --> 00:07:25,760
I'm telling you the Crown is six million in debt.

91
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,290
How could you let this happen?

92
00:07:27,470 --> 00:07:29,050
The Master of Coin finds the money.

93
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:31,630
The king and the Hand spend it.

94
00:07:31,630 --> 00:07:35,120
I will not believe Jon Arryn allowed Robert to bankrupt the realm.

95
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:38,460
Lord Arryn gave wise and prudent advice,

96
00:07:38,640 --> 00:07:42,040
but I fear His Grace doesn't always listen.

97
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:44,060
"Counting coppers," He calls it.

98
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:47,100
I'll speak to him tomorrow.

99
00:07:47,490 --> 00:07:50,080
This tournament is an extravagance we cannot afford.

100
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:52,050
As you will. But still, we'd best make our plans.

101
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:54,360
There will be no plans

102
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:56,220
until I speak to Robert.

103
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:02,600
Forgive me, my lords. I'm...

104
00:08:02,790 --> 00:08:05,970
- I had a long ride. - You are the King's Hand,

105
00:08:05,970 --> 00:08:09,710
Lord Stark, we serve at your pleasure.

106
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:19,140
Please, it's nearly healed.

107
00:08:21,010 --> 00:08:24,470
- It's ugly. - A king should have scars.

108
00:08:24,650 --> 00:08:28,250
You fought off a direwolf. You're a warrior like your father.

109
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:30,590
I'm not like him. I didn't fight off anything.

110
00:08:30,650 --> 00:08:32,420
It bit me and all I did was scream.

111
00:08:32,810 --> 00:08:34,920
And the two Stark girls saw it, both of them.

112
00:08:34,990 --> 00:08:38,130
That's not true. You killed the beast.

113
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:39,140
You only spared the girl

114
00:08:39,140 --> 00:08:41,290
because of the love your father bears her father.

115
00:08:41,350 --> 00:08:42,310
I didn't, I...

116
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:44,230
When Aerys Targaryen sat on the Iron Throne,

117
00:08:44,230 --> 00:08:46,540
your father was a rebel and a traitor.

118
00:08:47,730 --> 00:08:49,410
Someday you'll sit on the throne

119
00:08:49,410 --> 00:08:51,710
and the truth will be what you make it.

120
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:56,570
Do I have to marry her?

121
00:08:57,810 --> 00:08:59,240
Yes.

122
00:08:59,950 --> 00:09:02,420
She's very beautiful and young.

123
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:03,370
If you don't like her,

124
00:09:03,370 --> 00:09:05,320
you only need to see her on formal occasions

125
00:09:05,390 --> 00:09:09,270
and when the time comes, to make little princes and princesses.

126
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:12,620
And if you'd rather fuck painted whores,

127
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:14,490
you'll fuck painted whores.

128
00:09:15,020 --> 00:09:17,550
And if you'd rather lie with noble virgins, so be it.

129
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:18,880
You are my darling boy

130
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:21,810
and the world will be exactly as you want it to be.

131
00:09:25,370 --> 00:09:27,380
Do something nice for the Stark girl.

132
00:09:27,930 --> 00:09:29,980
- I don't want to. - No, but you will.

133
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:32,070
The occasional kindness will spare you

134
00:09:32,070 --> 00:09:34,070
all sorts of trouble down the road.

135
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,130
We allow the northerners too much power.

136
00:09:37,290 --> 00:09:39,570
They consider themselves our equals.

137
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,760
How would you handle them?

138
00:09:42,310 --> 00:09:44,080
I'd double their taxes

139
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:47,330
and command them to supply 10,000 men to the royal army.

140
00:09:47,330 --> 00:09:48,530
A royal army?

141
00:09:48,530 --> 00:09:50,490
Why should every lord command his own men?

142
00:09:50,550 --> 00:09:52,690
It's primitive, no better than the hill tribes.

143
00:09:52,690 --> 00:09:55,790
We should have a standing army of men loyal to the crown,

144
00:09:55,850 --> 00:09:57,690
trained by experienced soldiers...

145
00:09:57,750 --> 00:10:01,660
instead of a mob of peasants who've never held pikes in their lives.

146
00:10:02,430 --> 00:10:03,850
And if the northerners rebel?

147
00:10:03,920 --> 00:10:05,180
I'd crush them.

148
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:08,360
Seize Winterfell and install someone loyal to the realm

149
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:10,230
as warden of the north.

150
00:10:10,230 --> 00:10:11,340
Uncle Kevan, maybe.

151
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:13,030
And these 10,000 northern troops,

152
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:15,440
would they fight for you or their lord?

153
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:17,420
For me. I'm their King.

154
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:19,620
But you've just invaded their homeland,

155
00:10:19,690 --> 00:10:21,410
asked them to kill their brothers.

156
00:10:21,410 --> 00:10:22,350
I'm not asking.

157
00:10:22,420 --> 00:10:25,420
The north cannot be held... not by an outsider.

158
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:27,170
It's too big and too wild.

159
00:10:27,170 --> 00:10:29,320
And when the winter comes, the seven gods together

160
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:31,300
couldn't save you and your royal army.

161
00:10:31,740 --> 00:10:34,370
A good king knows when to save his strength...

162
00:10:36,170 --> 00:10:38,590
And when to destroy his enemies.

163
00:10:39,650 --> 00:10:41,370
So you agree...

164
00:10:41,950 --> 00:10:43,940
the Starks are enemies?

165
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:47,800
Everyone who isn't us

166
00:10:48,250 --> 00:10:49,850
is an enemy.

167
00:10:52,650 --> 00:10:55,120
Enough of that, young lady. Eat your food.

168
00:10:55,190 --> 00:10:56,180
I'm practicing.

169
00:10:56,180 --> 00:10:57,570
Practicing for what?

170
00:10:57,570 --> 00:10:59,550
- The prince. - Arya, stop!

171
00:10:59,550 --> 00:11:01,190
He's a liar and a coward

172
00:11:01,190 --> 00:11:02,450
and he killed my friend.

173
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:03,960
The Hound killed your friend.

174
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:06,420
The Hound does whatever the prince tells him to do.

175
00:11:06,490 --> 00:11:07,360
You're an idiot.

176
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:08,990
You're a liar, and if you told the truth

177
00:11:09,050 --> 00:11:10,360
Mycah would be alive.

178
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:11,940
Enough!

179
00:11:14,450 --> 00:11:15,770
What's happening here?

180
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:18,820
Arya would rather act like a beast than a lady.

181
00:11:20,190 --> 00:11:22,110
Go to your room. We'll speak later.

182
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:31,770
That's for you, love.

183
00:11:41,590 --> 00:11:44,740
The same dollmaker makes all of princess Myrcella's toys.

184
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:49,010
Don't you like it?

185
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:52,190
I haven't played with dolls since I was eight.

186
00:11:53,650 --> 00:11:54,990
May I be excused?

187
00:11:54,990 --> 00:11:56,670
You've barely eaten a thing.

188
00:11:57,710 --> 00:12:00,560
It's all right. Go on.

189
00:12:09,470 --> 00:12:11,610
War was easier than daughters.

190
00:12:17,590 --> 00:12:19,050
Go away!

191
00:12:19,050 --> 00:12:21,260
Arya, open the door.

192
00:12:31,070 --> 00:12:32,550
May I come in?

193
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:40,820
Whose sword is that?

194
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:42,220
Mine.

195
00:12:42,450 --> 00:12:43,880
Give it to me.

196
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:53,990
I know this maker's mark. This is Mikken's work.

197
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:58,010
Where did you get this?

198
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:03,420
This is no toy.

199
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:07,500
Little ladies shouldn't play with swords.

200
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:08,800
I wasn't playing.

201
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,060
And I don't want to be a lady.

202
00:13:11,610 --> 00:13:13,140
Come here.

203
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:20,660
Now what do you want with this?

204
00:13:20,790 --> 00:13:22,570
It's called Needle.

205
00:13:23,310 --> 00:13:25,750
Oh, a blade with a name.

206
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:29,250
And who were you hoping to skewer with Needle?

207
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:30,520
Your sister?

208
00:13:31,270 --> 00:13:33,700
Do you know the first thing about sword fighting?

209
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:35,720
Stick 'em with the pointy end.

210
00:13:36,830 --> 00:13:38,700
That's the essence of it.

211
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:43,480
I was trying to learn.

212
00:13:45,850 --> 00:13:48,720
I asked Mycah to practice with me.

213
00:13:49,990 --> 00:13:51,720
I asked him.

214
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:55,150
- It was my fault. - No, sweet girl.

215
00:13:55,220 --> 00:13:58,930
No no, you didn't kill the butcher's boy.

216
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:03,120
I hate them! I hate all of them.

217
00:14:03,190 --> 00:14:05,820
The Hound, the Queen and the King

218
00:14:05,890 --> 00:14:07,220
and Joffrey and Sansa.

219
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:09,890
Sansa was dragged before the king and queen...

220
00:14:11,090 --> 00:14:13,750
And asked to call the prince a liar.

221
00:14:13,820 --> 00:14:16,220
So was I! He is a liar.

222
00:14:16,290 --> 00:14:18,290
Shh, darling, listen to me.

223
00:14:19,890 --> 00:14:22,850
Sansa will be married to Joffrey's someday.

224
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:25,290
She cannot betray him.

225
00:14:25,290 --> 00:14:28,340
She must take his side even when he's wrong.

226
00:14:28,980 --> 00:14:32,060
But how you can let her marry someone like that?

227
00:14:37,550 --> 00:14:39,190
Look at me.

228
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:41,830
You're a Stark of Winterfell.

229
00:14:41,830 --> 00:14:43,670
You know our words.

230
00:14:45,670 --> 00:14:47,560
Winter is coming.

231
00:14:48,270 --> 00:14:50,560
You were born in the long summer.

232
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:52,650
You've never known anything else.

233
00:14:52,720 --> 00:14:54,440
But now winter is truly coming.

234
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:58,140
And in the winter, we must protect ourselves,

235
00:14:58,530 --> 00:15:02,290
look after one another. Sansa is your sister.

236
00:15:03,690 --> 00:15:05,660
I don't hate her.

237
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:08,590
Not really.

238
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:11,300
I don't want to frighten you,

239
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:13,270
but I won't lie to you either.

240
00:15:13,640 --> 00:15:16,090
We've come to a dangerous place.

241
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:19,410
We cannot fight a war amongst ourselves.

242
00:15:20,140 --> 00:15:21,680
All right?

243
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,940
Go on. It's yours.

244
00:15:28,980 --> 00:15:30,970
I can keep it?

245
00:15:31,550 --> 00:15:33,910
Try not to stab your sister with it.

246
00:15:42,670 --> 00:15:44,440
If you're going to own a sword,

247
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:46,740
you'd better know how to use it.

248
00:15:54,250 --> 00:15:58,280
Don't listen to it. Crows are all liars.

249
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:02,290
I know a story about a crow.

250
00:16:02,290 --> 00:16:04,120
I hate your stories.

251
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:08,030
I know a story about a boy who hated stories.

252
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:11,020
I could tell you about Ser Duncan the Tall.

253
00:16:11,090 --> 00:16:13,190
Those were always your favorites.

254
00:16:13,190 --> 00:16:15,080
Those weren't my favorites.

255
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,390
My favorites were the scary ones.

256
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:21,540
Oh, my sweet summer child.

257
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:24,020
What do you know about fear?

258
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:26,950
Fear is for the winter,

259
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:30,320
when the snows fall a hundred feet deep.

260
00:16:30,550 --> 00:16:32,510
Fear is for the long night,

261
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:35,120
when the sun hides for years,

262
00:16:35,190 --> 00:16:38,210
and children are born and live and die

263
00:16:38,210 --> 00:16:40,790
all in darkness.

264
00:16:40,790 --> 00:16:43,690
That is the time for fear, my little lord,

265
00:16:43,750 --> 00:16:47,060
when the white walkers move through the woods.

266
00:16:48,450 --> 00:16:50,310
Thousands of years ago

267
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:53,720
there came a night that lasted a generation.

268
00:16:53,790 --> 00:16:56,690
Kings froze to death in their castles,

269
00:16:56,750 --> 00:16:58,920
same as the shepherds in their huts.

270
00:16:59,210 --> 00:17:01,850
And women smothered their babies

271
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:03,750
rather than see them starve,

272
00:17:03,930 --> 00:17:08,620
and wept and felt the tears freeze on their cheeks.

273
00:17:09,150 --> 00:17:12,160
So is this the sort of story that you like?

274
00:17:15,370 --> 00:17:16,950
In that darkness,

275
00:17:17,020 --> 00:17:19,840
the white walkers came for the first time.

276
00:17:20,010 --> 00:17:22,650
They swept through cities and kingdoms,

277
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:24,890
riding their dead horses,

278
00:17:24,950 --> 00:17:29,740
hunting with their packs of pale spiders big as hounds...

279
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:35,150
What are you telling him now?

280
00:17:35,220 --> 00:17:37,620
Only what the little lord wants to hear.

281
00:17:37,690 --> 00:17:40,100
Get your supper. I want some time with him.

282
00:17:52,120 --> 00:17:53,800
One time she told me

283
00:17:54,350 --> 00:17:55,590
the sky is blue because we live inside the eye

284
00:17:55,590 --> 00:17:58,760
of a blue-eyed giant named Macomber.

285
00:17:58,760 --> 00:18:00,390
Maybe we do.

286
00:18:03,050 --> 00:18:04,560
How do you feel?

287
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:11,290
You still don't remember anything?

288
00:18:12,850 --> 00:18:14,260
Bran,

289
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:17,160
I've seen you climb a thousand times.

290
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:19,020
In the wind, in the rain...

291
00:18:19,230 --> 00:18:21,090
a thousand times.

292
00:18:21,090 --> 00:18:23,820
- You never fall. - I did though.

293
00:18:26,770 --> 00:18:29,150
It's true, isn't it,

294
00:18:29,510 --> 00:18:32,400
what Maester Luwin says about my legs?

295
00:18:40,090 --> 00:18:42,110
I'd rather be dead.

296
00:18:43,050 --> 00:18:46,490
- Don't ever say that. - I'd rather be dead.

297
00:18:58,140 --> 00:19:00,480
Fewer eyes back here, my lady.

298
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:02,650
But still too many.

299
00:19:02,650 --> 00:19:05,370
It's nine years since I've set foot in the capital.

300
00:19:05,370 --> 00:19:08,580
And no one knew who I was the last time I came either.

301
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:13,380
My lady.

302
00:19:14,750 --> 00:19:16,650
Welcome to King's Landing, Lady Stark.

303
00:19:16,650 --> 00:19:18,050
Would you mind following us?

304
00:19:18,050 --> 00:19:19,790
I would. We've done nothing wrong.

305
00:19:19,850 --> 00:19:22,070
We've been instructed to escort you into the city.

306
00:19:22,070 --> 00:19:23,870
Instructed?

307
00:19:23,870 --> 00:19:26,660
I don't know who's providing your instructions, but...

308
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:28,230
Follow me, Lady Stark.

309
00:19:39,460 --> 00:19:42,030
Cat! Go on.

310
00:19:42,030 --> 00:19:43,680
Go upstairs.

311
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:48,800
You little worm!

312
00:19:49,240 --> 00:19:51,690
You take me for some back-alley sally

313
00:19:51,750 --> 00:19:53,430
you can drag into a...

314
00:19:59,050 --> 00:20:01,120
I meant no disrespect

315
00:20:01,120 --> 00:20:03,490
to you of all people.

316
00:20:03,490 --> 00:20:05,620
How dare you bring me here!

317
00:20:05,890 --> 00:20:07,300
Have you lost your mind?

318
00:20:07,300 --> 00:20:08,520
No one will come looking for you here.

319
00:20:08,520 --> 00:20:09,850
Isn't that what you wanted?

320
00:20:09,850 --> 00:20:13,390
I'm truly sorry about the locale.

321
00:20:13,780 --> 00:20:16,210
How did you know I was coming to King's Landing?

322
00:20:17,150 --> 00:20:19,120
A dear friend told me.

323
00:20:20,780 --> 00:20:23,790
- Lady Stark. - Lord Varys.

324
00:20:23,810 --> 00:20:27,420
To see you again after so many years is a blessing.

325
00:20:27,450 --> 00:20:28,950
Your poor hands.

326
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:33,160
How did you know I was coming?

327
00:20:33,450 --> 00:20:35,570
Knowledge is my trade, my lady.

328
00:20:37,530 --> 00:20:39,910
Did you bring the dagger with you, by any chance?

329
00:20:41,510 --> 00:20:43,650
My little birds are everywhere...

330
00:20:44,020 --> 00:20:45,820
even in the north.

331
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:49,980
They whisper to me the strangest stories.

332
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:57,020
Valyrian steel.

333
00:20:57,180 --> 00:20:59,700
Do you know whose dagger this is?

334
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:03,200
I must admit I do not.

335
00:21:04,710 --> 00:21:07,630
Well well, this is an historic day.

336
00:21:08,190 --> 00:21:10,360
Something you don't know

337
00:21:10,570 --> 00:21:11,810
that I do.

338
00:21:14,130 --> 00:21:17,880
There's only one dagger like this in all of the Seven Kingdoms.

339
00:21:19,590 --> 00:21:22,150
- It's mine. - Yours?

340
00:21:22,300 --> 00:21:23,730
At least it was,

341
00:21:23,730 --> 00:21:26,650
until the tournament on prince Joffrey's last nameday.

342
00:21:27,380 --> 00:21:29,400
I bet on ser Jaime in the jousting,

343
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:31,050
as any sane man would.

344
00:21:31,110 --> 00:21:33,480
When the Knight of the Flowers unseated him,

345
00:21:34,860 --> 00:21:36,430
I lost this dagger.

346
00:21:36,570 --> 00:21:37,490
To whom?

347
00:21:38,610 --> 00:21:40,210
Tyrion Lannister.

348
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:42,170
The Imp.

349
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:45,560
Grenn, show him what you farm boys are made of.

350
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:52,900
If that were a real sword, you'd be dead.

351
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:57,040
Lord Snow here grew up in a castle

352
00:21:57,040 --> 00:21:59,050
spitting down on the likes of you.

353
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:01,150
Pyp.

354
00:22:01,660 --> 00:22:03,600
Do you think Ned Stark's bastard

355
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:05,490
bleeds like the rest of us?

356
00:22:13,730 --> 00:22:14,650
Next!

357
00:22:25,990 --> 00:22:26,970
Next!

358
00:22:40,770 --> 00:22:42,010
Well, Lord Snow,

359
00:22:42,140 --> 00:22:44,720
it appears you're the least useless person here.

360
00:22:46,190 --> 00:22:47,820
Go clean yourselves up.

361
00:22:48,370 --> 00:22:50,460
There's only so much I can stomach in a day.

362
00:22:50,940 --> 00:22:52,090
A charming man.

363
00:22:53,130 --> 00:22:54,900
I don't need him to be charming.

364
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:58,870
I need him to turn this bunch of thieves and runaways

365
00:22:58,870 --> 00:23:00,600
into men of the Night's Watch.

366
00:23:00,860 --> 00:23:02,970
And how's that going, Commander Mormont?

367
00:23:03,570 --> 00:23:04,580
Slowly.

368
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:08,870
A raven came

369
00:23:09,260 --> 00:23:10,850
for Ned Stark's son.

370
00:23:15,090 --> 00:23:16,560
Good news or bad?

371
00:23:17,300 --> 00:23:18,360
Both.

372
00:23:20,290 --> 00:23:21,430
Lord Stark.

373
00:23:23,710 --> 00:23:26,650
I meant to give you this earlier.

374
00:23:28,540 --> 00:23:30,460
So forgetful these days.

375
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:35,260
A raven from Winterfell this morning.

376
00:23:46,230 --> 00:23:47,660
Good news?

377
00:23:51,870 --> 00:23:54,020
Perhaps you'd like to share it with your wife?

378
00:23:56,810 --> 00:23:59,100
- My wife is in Winterfell. - Is she?

379
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:10,080
Yes, I'm looking at you.

380
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:14,490
I thought that she'd be safest in here.

381
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:17,780
One of several such establishments I own.

382
00:24:20,220 --> 00:24:21,440
You're a funny man.

383
00:24:22,020 --> 00:24:24,540
Huh? A very funny man.

384
00:24:25,970 --> 00:24:26,980
Ned!

385
00:24:34,430 --> 00:24:35,860
Ah, the Starks...

386
00:24:36,960 --> 00:24:39,410
quick tempers, slow minds.

387
00:24:44,590 --> 00:24:46,210
You broke my nose, bastard!

388
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,460
It's an improvement.

389
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:00,950
If we threw you over the wall,

390
00:25:00,950 --> 00:25:02,540
I wonder how long it would take you to hit.

391
00:25:02,540 --> 00:25:04,780
I wonder if they'd find you before the wolves did.

392
00:25:09,460 --> 00:25:10,990
What're you looking at, half man?

393
00:25:12,340 --> 00:25:13,540
I'm looking at you.

394
00:25:15,160 --> 00:25:16,210
Yes.

395
00:25:16,870 --> 00:25:19,460
You've got an interesting face.

396
00:25:20,240 --> 00:25:23,790
Hmm, very distinctive faces.

397
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:24,920
All of you.

398
00:25:26,120 --> 00:25:28,110
And what do you care about our faces?

399
00:25:28,150 --> 00:25:31,100
It's just I think they would look marvelous

400
00:25:31,100 --> 00:25:33,380
decorating spikes in King's Landing.

401
00:25:33,660 --> 00:25:36,360
Perhaps I'll write my sister, the Queen, about it.

402
00:25:39,320 --> 00:25:40,820
We'll talk later, Lord Snow.

403
00:25:47,520 --> 00:25:49,660
Everybody knew what this place was

404
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:51,090
and no one told me.

405
00:25:51,710 --> 00:25:52,680
No one but you.

406
00:25:53,830 --> 00:25:55,120
My father knew

407
00:25:55,830 --> 00:25:58,200
and he left me to rot at the Wall all the same.

408
00:25:58,200 --> 00:25:59,970
Grenn's father left him too...

409
00:26:00,640 --> 00:26:03,100
Outside a farmhouse when he was three.

410
00:26:03,990 --> 00:26:07,750
Pyp was caught stealing a wheel of cheese.

411
00:26:07,750 --> 00:26:10,450
His little sister hadn't eaten in three days.

412
00:26:11,550 --> 00:26:14,270
He was given a choice: his right hand or the wall.

413
00:26:14,440 --> 00:26:16,510
I've been asking the Lord Commander about them.

414
00:26:16,510 --> 00:26:18,400
Fascinating stories.

415
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:20,380
They hate me because I'm better than they are.

416
00:26:20,380 --> 00:26:21,860
It's a lucky thing none of them were trained

417
00:26:21,860 --> 00:26:24,950
by a master-at-arms like your Ser Rodrik.

418
00:26:24,950 --> 00:26:27,500
I don't imagine any of them have ever held a real sword

419
00:26:27,500 --> 00:26:28,890
before they came here.

420
00:26:35,230 --> 00:26:36,500
Your brother Bran.

421
00:26:38,100 --> 00:26:39,210
He's woken up.

422
00:26:41,780 --> 00:26:43,520
The mere suggestion that the Queen's brother

423
00:26:43,520 --> 00:26:45,870
tried to kill your boy would be considered treason.

424
00:26:45,870 --> 00:26:48,060
We have proof. We have the blade.

425
00:26:48,060 --> 00:26:50,370
Which Lord Tyrion will say was stolen from him.

426
00:26:50,370 --> 00:26:52,850
The only man who could say otherwise has no throat,

427
00:26:52,850 --> 00:26:54,310
thanks to your boy's wolf.

428
00:26:55,310 --> 00:26:58,510
Petyr has promised to help us find the truth.

429
00:26:59,310 --> 00:27:01,210
He's like a little brother to me, Ned.

430
00:27:01,210 --> 00:27:03,410
He would never betray my trust.

431
00:27:03,650 --> 00:27:06,190
I'll try to keep you alive, for her sake.

432
00:27:06,370 --> 00:27:07,790
A fool's task, admittedly,

433
00:27:07,790 --> 00:27:10,750
but I've never been able to refuse your wife anything.

434
00:27:10,940 --> 00:27:12,290
I won't forget this.

435
00:27:13,330 --> 00:27:14,850
You're a true friend.

436
00:27:15,250 --> 00:27:18,870
Don't tell anyone. I have a reputation to maintain.

437
00:27:22,470 --> 00:27:24,780
- How could you be so stupid? - Calm down.

438
00:27:24,780 --> 00:27:27,470
He's a child... 10 years old.

439
00:27:27,470 --> 00:27:29,510
- What were you thinking? - I was thinking of us.

440
00:27:29,510 --> 00:27:31,750
You're a bit late to start complaining about it now.

441
00:27:32,560 --> 00:27:34,160
- What has the boy told them? - Nothing.

442
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:36,210
He's said nothing. He remembers nothing.

443
00:27:36,210 --> 00:27:38,160
Then what are you raving about?

444
00:27:38,160 --> 00:27:39,480
What if it comes back to him?

445
00:27:40,310 --> 00:27:41,740
If he tells his father what he saw...

446
00:27:41,740 --> 00:27:43,870
We'll say he was lying. We'll say he was dreaming.

447
00:27:43,870 --> 00:27:45,680
We'll say whatever we like.

448
00:27:45,680 --> 00:27:47,870
I think we can outfox a 10-year-old.

449
00:27:47,870 --> 00:27:51,310
- And my husband? - I'll go to war with him if I have to.

450
00:27:51,760 --> 00:27:54,020
They can write a ballad about us:

451
00:27:54,040 --> 00:27:56,080
"The war for Cersei's cunt."

452
00:28:01,230 --> 00:28:02,780
- Let me go. - Never.

453
00:28:03,540 --> 00:28:07,560
- Let me go. - The boy won't talk.

454
00:28:07,950 --> 00:28:09,590
And if he does, I'll kill him.

455
00:28:10,070 --> 00:28:13,160
Him, Ned Stark, the King... the whole bloody lot of them,

456
00:28:13,160 --> 00:28:17,930
until you and I are the only people Left in this world.

457
00:28:29,380 --> 00:28:31,150
I wish I could see the girls.

458
00:28:31,540 --> 00:28:34,780
- It's too dangerous. - Just for a moment.

459
00:28:34,780 --> 00:28:36,810
Until we know who our enemies are...

460
00:28:36,810 --> 00:28:38,960
I know they did it, Ned. The Lannisters.

461
00:28:38,960 --> 00:28:40,650
In my bones, I know it.

462
00:28:40,860 --> 00:28:42,540
Littlefinger's right.

463
00:28:44,850 --> 00:28:46,930
I can't do anything without proof.

464
00:28:46,930 --> 00:28:48,870
And if you find the proof?

465
00:28:49,510 --> 00:28:50,960
Then I bring it to Robert...

466
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:54,210
and hope he's still the man I once knew.

467
00:28:56,250 --> 00:28:57,960
You watch yourself on the road, huh?

468
00:28:59,500 --> 00:29:01,580
That temper of yours is a dangerous thing.

469
00:29:01,580 --> 00:29:04,680
My temper? Gods be good,

470
00:29:04,680 --> 00:29:07,090
you nearly killed poor Littlefinger yesterday.

471
00:29:12,190 --> 00:29:13,390
He still loves you.

472
00:29:15,180 --> 00:29:16,120
Does he?

473
00:29:35,220 --> 00:29:36,260
Off with you.

474
00:30:08,400 --> 00:30:11,500
Yes, it's been a long time.

475
00:30:12,660 --> 00:30:15,070
But I still remember every face.

476
00:30:16,950 --> 00:30:18,740
You remember your first?

477
00:30:21,350 --> 00:30:22,610
Of course, Your Grace.

478
00:30:23,730 --> 00:30:24,740
Who was it?

479
00:30:25,970 --> 00:30:27,040
A Tyroshi.

480
00:30:27,890 --> 00:30:29,780
- Never learned the name. - Hmm.

481
00:30:31,150 --> 00:30:32,270
How'd you do it?

482
00:30:32,780 --> 00:30:34,200
Lance through the heart.

483
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:36,160
Quick one.

484
00:30:37,650 --> 00:30:38,700
Lucky for you.

485
00:30:40,280 --> 00:30:44,440
Mine was some Tarly boy at the battle of Summerhall.

486
00:30:45,700 --> 00:30:48,350
My horse took an arrow so I was on foot,

487
00:30:48,350 --> 00:30:49,800
slogging through the mud.

488
00:30:51,530 --> 00:30:56,530
He came running at me, this dumb high-born lad,

489
00:30:57,090 --> 00:30:58,810
thinking he could end the rebellion

490
00:30:58,810 --> 00:31:01,450
with a single swing of his sword.

491
00:31:02,870 --> 00:31:04,750
I knocked him down with the hammer.

492
00:31:04,750 --> 00:31:07,230
Gods, I was strong then.

493
00:31:07,620 --> 00:31:10,040
Caved in his breastplate.

494
00:31:10,920 --> 00:31:13,530
Probably shattered every rib he had.

495
00:31:14,310 --> 00:31:17,420
Stood over him, hammer in the air.

496
00:31:18,060 --> 00:31:22,730
Right before I brought it down he shouted, "Wait! Wait."

497
00:31:29,100 --> 00:31:32,350
They never tell you how they all shit themselves.

498
00:31:34,430 --> 00:31:37,050
They don't put that part in the songs.

499
00:31:39,770 --> 00:31:41,290
Stupid boy.

500
00:31:43,540 --> 00:31:48,160
Now the Tarlys bend the knee like everyone else.

501
00:31:49,100 --> 00:31:50,450
He could have lingered

502
00:31:50,450 --> 00:31:53,080
on the edge of the battle with the smart boys

503
00:31:53,080 --> 00:31:57,120
and today his wife would be making him miserable,

504
00:31:57,510 --> 00:31:59,750
his sons would be ingrates,

505
00:32:00,210 --> 00:32:02,880
and he'd be waking three times in the night

506
00:32:02,880 --> 00:32:05,710
to piss into a bowl. Wine!

507
00:32:09,090 --> 00:32:13,920
Lancel. Gods, what a stupid name.

508
00:32:14,840 --> 00:32:17,270
Lancel Lannister.

509
00:32:18,600 --> 00:32:22,840
Who named you? Some halfwit with a stutter?

510
00:32:25,550 --> 00:32:26,600
What are you doing?

511
00:32:28,800 --> 00:32:31,590
- It's empty, Your Grace. - What do you mean it's empty?

512
00:32:31,590 --> 00:32:34,620
- there's no more wine. - Is that what empty means?

513
00:32:36,450 --> 00:32:39,480
So get more.

514
00:32:42,980 --> 00:32:45,290
Tell your cousin to get in here.

515
00:32:45,290 --> 00:32:46,540
Kingslayer!

516
00:32:46,860 --> 00:32:48,010
Get in here.

517
00:32:55,700 --> 00:32:58,270
Surrounded by Lannisters.

518
00:32:59,150 --> 00:33:02,690
Every time I close my eyes I see their blond hair

519
00:33:02,690 --> 00:33:06,480
and their smug, satisfied faces.

520
00:33:07,110 --> 00:33:09,270
It must wound your pride, huh?

521
00:33:09,270 --> 00:33:12,420
Standing out there like a glorified sentry.

522
00:33:13,660 --> 00:33:17,380
Jaime Lannister, son of the mighty Tywin...

523
00:33:18,710 --> 00:33:21,190
Forced to mind the door while your king

524
00:33:21,190 --> 00:33:23,900
eats and drinks and shits and fucks.

525
00:33:26,120 --> 00:33:27,050
So come on.

526
00:33:27,510 --> 00:33:29,540
We're telling war stories.

527
00:33:31,190 --> 00:33:34,430
Who was your first kill, not counting old men?

528
00:33:36,250 --> 00:33:38,430
One of the outlaws in the brotherhood.

529
00:33:39,110 --> 00:33:40,890
I was there that day.

530
00:33:41,370 --> 00:33:44,590
You were only a squire, 16 years old.

531
00:33:44,820 --> 00:33:47,560
You killed Simon Toyne with a counter riposte.

532
00:33:47,570 --> 00:33:48,970
Best move I ever saw.

533
00:33:50,470 --> 00:33:54,260
A good fighter, Toyne, but he lacked stamina.

534
00:33:54,680 --> 00:33:55,830
Your outlaw...

535
00:33:57,210 --> 00:33:58,650
any last words?

536
00:33:58,650 --> 00:34:01,270
I cut his head off, so no.

537
00:34:02,100 --> 00:34:04,150
What about Aerys Targaryen?

538
00:34:04,880 --> 00:34:08,760
What did the mad king say when you stabbed him in the back?

539
00:34:09,040 --> 00:34:10,190
I never asked.

540
00:34:11,420 --> 00:34:13,330
Did he call you a traitor?

541
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:16,540
Did he plead for a reprieve?

542
00:34:18,530 --> 00:34:21,240
He said the same thing he'd been saying for hours...

543
00:34:22,840 --> 00:34:24,190
"Burn them all."

544
00:34:29,940 --> 00:34:31,440
If that's all, Your Grace...

545
00:35:04,370 --> 00:35:06,600
Do the Dothraki buy their slaves?

546
00:35:06,950 --> 00:35:08,690
The Dothraki don't believe in money.

547
00:35:08,900 --> 00:35:11,310
Most of their slaves were given to them as gifts.

548
00:35:11,310 --> 00:35:13,840
- From whom? - If you rule a city

549
00:35:13,840 --> 00:35:16,380
and you see the horde approaching, you have two choices:

550
00:35:16,380 --> 00:35:18,020
Pay tribute or fight.

551
00:35:18,480 --> 00:35:20,160
An easy choice for most.

552
00:35:21,580 --> 00:35:23,550
Of course, sometimes it's not enough.

553
00:35:23,860 --> 00:35:24,990
Sometimes a khal feels

554
00:35:24,990 --> 00:35:27,330
insulted by the number of slaves he's given.

555
00:35:27,540 --> 00:35:29,900
He might think the men too weak or the women too ugly.

556
00:35:30,050 --> 00:35:31,360
Sometimes a khal decides

557
00:35:31,360 --> 00:35:34,910
his riders haven't had a good fight in months and need the practice

558
00:35:34,910 --> 00:35:36,930
kash qoy qoyi thira disse.

559
00:35:39,770 --> 00:35:41,070
Tell them all to stop.

560
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:43,440
You want the entire horde to stop?

561
00:35:43,990 --> 00:35:44,970
For how long?

562
00:35:46,510 --> 00:35:48,880
Until I command them otherwise.

563
00:35:49,710 --> 00:35:51,590
You're learning to talk like a queen.

564
00:35:52,180 --> 00:35:53,290
Not a queen.

565
00:35:54,560 --> 00:35:55,740
A Khaleesi.

566
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:08,970
Annakhas dozgosores.

567
00:36:33,260 --> 00:36:34,820
You dare!

568
00:36:35,190 --> 00:36:38,130
You give commands to me? To me?

569
00:36:40,190 --> 00:36:44,040
You do not command the dragon. I am Lord of the Seven Kingdoms.

570
00:36:44,040 --> 00:36:47,400
I don't take orders from savages or their sluts.

571
00:36:47,400 --> 00:36:48,950
Do you hear me?

572
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:54,440
Hash shafka zali nharees, zhey Khaleesi?

573
00:36:54,890 --> 00:36:57,570
- Rakharo ask if you want him dead, Khaleesi. - No.

574
00:36:58,430 --> 00:37:01,530
Ishish chare acharoe hash me nem ervae, nharesoon.

575
00:37:01,910 --> 00:37:04,260
Rakharo say you should take ear, to teach respect.

576
00:37:04,660 --> 00:37:07,170
Please please, don't hurt him.

577
00:37:11,470 --> 00:37:15,680
Tell him I don't want my brother harmed.

578
00:37:15,680 --> 00:37:17,810
Khaleesi vos zalo meme nem azisa.

579
00:37:21,220 --> 00:37:22,420
Shafki.

580
00:37:27,920 --> 00:37:31,470
Mormont! Kill these Dothraki dogs!

581
00:37:37,020 --> 00:37:39,410
I am your King!

582
00:37:40,850 --> 00:37:43,520
Shall we return to the Khalasar, Khaleesi?

583
00:38:06,470 --> 00:38:09,220
You walk.

584
00:40:39,320 --> 00:40:43,440
I wanted to be here when you saw it for the first time.

585
00:40:51,800 --> 00:40:54,900
- I'm leaving this morning. - You're leaving?

586
00:40:56,020 --> 00:40:57,280
I'm the first ranger.

587
00:40:58,250 --> 00:40:59,540
My job is out there.

588
00:41:01,310 --> 00:41:04,470
- There have been disturbing reports. - What kind of reports?

589
00:41:04,540 --> 00:41:05,990
The kind I don't want to believe.

590
00:41:07,390 --> 00:41:09,760
I'm ready. I won't let you down.

591
00:41:10,880 --> 00:41:11,880
You're not going.

592
00:41:15,120 --> 00:41:16,440
You're no ranger, Jon.

593
00:41:17,030 --> 00:41:19,210
- But I'm better than every... - Better than no one!

594
00:41:24,710 --> 00:41:25,950
Here...

595
00:41:26,760 --> 00:41:28,460
A man gets what he earns,

596
00:41:29,210 --> 00:41:30,720
when he earns it.

597
00:41:35,620 --> 00:41:36,900
We'll speak when I return.

598
00:41:52,840 --> 00:41:55,830
- A bear's balls. - Oh, you're joking?

599
00:41:55,830 --> 00:41:59,670
And his brains and his guts, his lungs and his heart,

600
00:41:59,820 --> 00:42:02,080
all fried in his own fat.

601
00:42:02,080 --> 00:42:04,840
When you're a hundred miles north of the Wall

602
00:42:04,840 --> 00:42:06,520
and you ate your last meal a week ago,

603
00:42:06,520 --> 00:42:08,590
you leave nothing for the wolves.

604
00:42:09,040 --> 00:42:11,780
And how do a bear's balls taste?

605
00:42:11,780 --> 00:42:13,060
A bit chewy.

606
00:42:16,190 --> 00:42:17,480
And what about you, my Lord?

607
00:42:17,480 --> 00:42:19,580
What's the strangest thing you've eaten?

608
00:42:20,250 --> 00:42:22,260
Do Dornish girls count?

609
00:42:25,870 --> 00:42:29,190
So you roam the Seven Kingdoms,

610
00:42:29,190 --> 00:42:31,630
collaring pickpockets and horse thieves

611
00:42:31,630 --> 00:42:33,480
and bringing them here as eager recruits?

612
00:42:33,480 --> 00:42:34,570
Aye.

613
00:42:35,010 --> 00:42:38,300
But it's not all of 'em's done bad things.

614
00:42:38,300 --> 00:42:41,410
Some of 'em's just poor lads looking for steady feed.

615
00:42:41,440 --> 00:42:44,360
Some of 'em's high-born lads looking for glory.

616
00:42:44,360 --> 00:42:46,680
They have a better chance finding feed than glory.

617
00:42:49,030 --> 00:42:51,020
The Night's Watch is a joke to you, is it?

618
00:42:52,340 --> 00:42:54,060
Is that what we are, Lannister?

619
00:42:54,680 --> 00:42:56,760
An army of jesters in black?

620
00:42:57,000 --> 00:42:58,630
You don't have enough men to be an army

621
00:42:58,630 --> 00:43:01,470
and aside from you're here, none of you are particularly funny.

622
00:43:03,030 --> 00:43:05,310
I hope we've provided you with some good stories to tell

623
00:43:05,310 --> 00:43:07,130
when you're back in King's Landing.

624
00:43:07,440 --> 00:43:10,780
But something to think about while you're drinking your wine down there,

625
00:43:11,180 --> 00:43:12,710
enjoying your brothels.

626
00:43:14,140 --> 00:43:16,990
Half the boys you've seen training will die north of the Wall.

627
00:43:18,280 --> 00:43:20,450
Might be a wilding's axe that gets them,

628
00:43:21,160 --> 00:43:22,570
might be sickness,

629
00:43:23,580 --> 00:43:25,530
might just be the cold.

630
00:43:26,820 --> 00:43:28,050
They die in pain.

631
00:43:29,410 --> 00:43:32,680
And they do it, so plump little lords like you

632
00:43:32,680 --> 00:43:36,080
can enjoy their summer afternoons in peace and comfort.

633
00:43:38,960 --> 00:43:40,210
Do you think I'm plump?

634
00:43:44,450 --> 00:43:46,630
Listen, Benjen... may I call you Benjen?

635
00:43:46,630 --> 00:43:47,700
Call me what you like.

636
00:43:47,760 --> 00:43:49,700
I'm not sure what I've done to offend you.

637
00:43:50,170 --> 00:43:52,300
I have great admiration for the Night's Watch.

638
00:43:52,300 --> 00:43:54,440
I've great admiration for you as first ranger.

639
00:43:54,440 --> 00:43:56,410
You know, my brother once told me

640
00:43:56,860 --> 00:43:59,490
that nothing someone says before the word "but"

641
00:43:59,490 --> 00:44:00,670
really counts.

642
00:44:01,840 --> 00:44:03,190
But...

643
00:44:04,540 --> 00:44:07,860
I don't believe that giants and ghouls and white walkers

644
00:44:07,860 --> 00:44:09,800
are lurking beyond the Wall.

645
00:44:10,010 --> 00:44:13,550
I believe that the only difference between us and the wildlings is that

646
00:44:13,550 --> 00:44:15,890
when that wall went up, our ancestors happened

647
00:44:15,890 --> 00:44:17,890
to live on the right side of it.

648
00:44:18,750 --> 00:44:19,790
You're right.

649
00:44:22,460 --> 00:44:24,560
The wildlings are no different from us.

650
00:44:25,170 --> 00:44:26,890
A little rougher maybe.

651
00:44:27,240 --> 00:44:29,300
But they're made of meat and bone.

652
00:44:29,920 --> 00:44:31,940
I know how to track them and I know how to kill them.

653
00:44:33,260 --> 00:44:36,460
It's not the wildlings giving me sleepless nights.

654
00:44:37,540 --> 00:44:39,570
You've never been north of the Wall,

655
00:44:39,670 --> 00:44:41,540
so don't tell me what's out there.

656
00:44:45,700 --> 00:44:46,950
Are you going below?

657
00:44:49,130 --> 00:44:52,480
- Keep well, keep warm. - Enjoy the capital, brother.

658
00:44:52,480 --> 00:44:54,210
Oh, I always do.

659
00:45:03,590 --> 00:45:06,050
I think he's starting to like me.

660
00:45:09,380 --> 00:45:12,270
- "Going below"? - Aye.

661
00:45:12,560 --> 00:45:15,320
Into the tunnel and out the other side.

662
00:45:16,280 --> 00:45:18,600
He'll be north of the wall for a month or two.

663
00:45:20,770 --> 00:45:23,630
So you're heading down to King's Landing too.

664
00:45:23,770 --> 00:45:26,530
Aye, day after tomorrow.

665
00:45:27,350 --> 00:45:30,730
I get about half of my recruits from their dungeons.

666
00:45:30,760 --> 00:45:34,860
Let's share the road. I could use some decent company.

667
00:45:35,140 --> 00:45:39,710
I... I travel a bit on the grubby side, my Lord.

668
00:45:39,710 --> 00:45:43,920
Not this time. We'll be staying at the finest castles and inns.

669
00:45:43,930 --> 00:45:45,870
No one turns away a Lannister.

670
00:45:52,150 --> 00:45:54,220
At jakar?

671
00:45:54,350 --> 00:45:55,850
Athjahakar.

672
00:45:56,230 --> 00:45:58,570
Ath ja haker.

673
00:45:58,670 --> 00:46:00,190
Athjahakar.

674
00:46:00,310 --> 00:46:01,780
Athjahakar.

675
00:46:02,140 --> 00:46:03,360
Yes, Khaleesi.

676
00:46:05,820 --> 00:46:08,090
Oh, what are you doing?

677
00:46:08,320 --> 00:46:10,420
When was last time you bleed, Khaleesi?

678
00:46:13,100 --> 00:46:14,870
You change, Khaleesi.

679
00:46:23,850 --> 00:46:25,960
For a man on horseback,

680
00:46:25,960 --> 00:46:28,000
the curved blade is a good thing,

681
00:46:28,390 --> 00:46:29,680
easier to handle.

682
00:46:30,460 --> 00:46:32,920
It's a good weapon for a Dothrakan.

683
00:46:34,140 --> 00:46:35,800
But a man in full plate...

684
00:46:35,800 --> 00:46:37,590
Shori tawakof.

685
00:46:38,410 --> 00:46:40,410
The arakh won't get through the steel.

686
00:46:41,810 --> 00:46:43,850
That's where the broadsword has the advantage.

687
00:46:44,550 --> 00:46:47,130
Designed for piercing plate.

688
00:46:51,620 --> 00:46:54,100
- Armor. - Armor.

689
00:46:54,490 --> 00:46:56,890
Armor make a man...

690
00:46:57,620 --> 00:46:59,320
- Vroz? - Slow.

691
00:46:59,320 --> 00:47:00,990
- Slow. - It's true,

692
00:47:01,290 --> 00:47:03,420
but it also keeps a man alive.

693
00:47:23,160 --> 00:47:24,370
He still is.

694
00:47:25,680 --> 00:47:26,990
A man of great honor

695
00:47:28,300 --> 00:47:29,510
and I betrayed him.

696
00:47:53,210 --> 00:47:56,010
I don't think she wants to eat dog.

697
00:47:59,230 --> 00:48:01,470
The khaleesi have baby inside her.

698
00:48:03,210 --> 00:48:06,950
It is true. She does not bleed for two moons.

699
00:48:07,260 --> 00:48:08,880
Her belly start to swell.

700
00:48:13,670 --> 00:48:15,270
She does not want to eat horse.

701
00:48:16,310 --> 00:48:19,240
I'll have the boys butcher a goat for supper.

702
00:48:24,770 --> 00:48:26,900
I need to ride to Qohor.

703
00:48:30,300 --> 00:48:33,850
Uh, we ride for Vaes Dothrak.

704
00:48:33,850 --> 00:48:36,140
Don't worry. I'll catch you.

705
00:48:36,600 --> 00:48:38,270
The horde's easy to find.

706
00:48:50,120 --> 00:48:51,630
Don't stand so still.

707
00:48:52,190 --> 00:48:54,120
It's harder to hit a moving target.

708
00:48:58,910 --> 00:49:01,730
Except for you. You move too much.

709
00:49:01,900 --> 00:49:04,750
I could just hold my sword out and let you do the work for me.

710
00:49:09,970 --> 00:49:12,650
How many winters have you seen, Lord Tyrion?

711
00:49:13,090 --> 00:49:15,840
Eight... no, nine.

712
00:49:15,840 --> 00:49:17,250
All of them brief?

713
00:49:17,310 --> 00:49:19,540
They say the winter of my birth

714
00:49:19,540 --> 00:49:21,570
was three years long, Maester Aemon.

715
00:49:21,570 --> 00:49:23,930
This summer has lasted nine.

716
00:49:24,760 --> 00:49:28,840
But reports from the Citadel tell us the days grow shorter.

717
00:49:28,840 --> 00:49:31,040
The Starks are always right eventually:

718
00:49:31,400 --> 00:49:33,590
Winter is coming.

719
00:49:34,510 --> 00:49:36,390
This one will be long

720
00:49:37,400 --> 00:49:40,050
and dark things will come with it.

721
00:49:40,050 --> 00:49:42,540
We've been capturing wildlings,

722
00:49:42,640 --> 00:49:45,930
more every month. They're fleeing south.

723
00:49:45,930 --> 00:49:50,120
The ones who flee say they've seen the white walkers.

724
00:49:50,120 --> 00:49:53,450
Yes, and the fishermen of Lannisport say they see mermaids.

725
00:49:53,450 --> 00:49:57,420
One of our own rangers swore he saw them kill his companions.

726
00:49:57,440 --> 00:49:59,210
He swore it right up to the moment

727
00:49:59,210 --> 00:50:01,400
Ned Stark chopped his head off.

728
00:50:01,810 --> 00:50:03,870
The Night's Watch is the only thing

729
00:50:03,870 --> 00:50:07,830
standing between the realm and what lies beyond.

730
00:50:08,290 --> 00:50:09,940
And it has has become an army

731
00:50:09,940 --> 00:50:13,790
of undisciplined boys and tired old men.

732
00:50:14,220 --> 00:50:16,710
There are less than a thousand of us now.

733
00:50:17,800 --> 00:50:20,640
We can't man the other castles on the Wall.

734
00:50:20,740 --> 00:50:23,800
We can't properly patrol the wilderness.

735
00:50:23,800 --> 00:50:25,250
We've barely enough resources

736
00:50:25,250 --> 00:50:27,880
to keep our lads armed and fed.

737
00:50:27,920 --> 00:50:29,900
Your sister

738
00:50:30,030 --> 00:50:32,090
sits by the side the King.

739
00:50:33,580 --> 00:50:36,590
Tell her we need help.

740
00:50:36,590 --> 00:50:38,140
When winter does come,

741
00:50:38,550 --> 00:50:41,320
Gods help us all if we're not ready.

742
00:51:48,180 --> 00:51:50,210
I'm sorry to see you leave, Lannister.

743
00:51:52,550 --> 00:51:54,200
It's either me or this cold.

744
00:51:54,550 --> 00:51:56,580
And it doesn't appear to be going anywhere.

745
00:51:57,510 --> 00:51:59,680
Will you stop at Winterfell on your way south?

746
00:51:59,690 --> 00:52:00,810
I expect I will.

747
00:52:01,210 --> 00:52:02,930
Gods know there aren't many feather beds

748
00:52:02,930 --> 00:52:04,600
between here and King's Landing.

749
00:52:05,130 --> 00:52:06,570
If you see my brother Bran,

750
00:52:08,400 --> 00:52:09,490
tell him I miss him.

751
00:52:10,870 --> 00:52:13,550
- Tell him I'd visit if I could. - Of course.

752
00:52:14,660 --> 00:52:15,840
He'll never walk again.

753
00:52:16,460 --> 00:52:17,980
If you're going to be a cripple,

754
00:52:18,290 --> 00:52:19,890
it's better to be a rich cripple.

755
00:52:21,530 --> 00:52:22,620
You take care, Snow.

756
00:52:23,080 --> 00:52:24,120
Farewell, my Lord.

757
00:52:36,070 --> 00:52:38,470
You are late, boy.

758
00:52:40,920 --> 00:52:43,150
Tomorrow you will be here at midday.

759
00:52:43,670 --> 00:52:44,790
Who are you?

760
00:52:46,290 --> 00:52:48,320
Your dancing master,

761
00:52:48,320 --> 00:52:49,890
Syrio Forel.

762
00:52:53,870 --> 00:52:55,480
Tomorrow you will catch it.

763
00:52:55,720 --> 00:52:57,030
Now pick it up.

764
00:52:59,640 --> 00:53:01,910
That is not the way, boy.

765
00:53:02,280 --> 00:53:05,840
This is not a greatsword that is needing two hands to swing it.

766
00:53:06,870 --> 00:53:10,170
- It's too heavy. - It is heavy as it needs to be

767
00:53:10,170 --> 00:53:11,860
to make you strong.

768
00:53:13,130 --> 00:53:14,140
Just so.

769
00:53:14,800 --> 00:53:16,950
One hand is all that is needed.

770
00:53:18,880 --> 00:53:20,520
Now you are standing all wrong.

771
00:53:20,520 --> 00:53:22,410
Turn your body sideface.

772
00:53:23,350 --> 00:53:24,430
Yes.

773
00:53:25,770 --> 00:53:26,780
So.

774
00:53:27,950 --> 00:53:30,260
You are skinny. That is good.

775
00:53:30,640 --> 00:53:32,680
The target is smaller.

776
00:53:33,080 --> 00:53:34,550
Now the grip... let me see.

777
00:53:36,380 --> 00:53:37,540
Yes.

778
00:53:38,270 --> 00:53:40,530
The grip must be delicate.

779
00:53:41,900 --> 00:53:43,090
What if I drop it?

780
00:53:43,730 --> 00:53:45,850
The steel must be part of your arm.

781
00:53:46,190 --> 00:53:48,640
Can you drop part of your arm? No.

782
00:53:48,710 --> 00:53:50,920
Nine years Syrio Forel was first sword

783
00:53:50,920 --> 00:53:53,370
to the Sealord of Braavos.

784
00:53:53,370 --> 00:53:56,620
He knows these things. You must listen to me, boy.

785
00:53:56,620 --> 00:53:57,730
I'm a girl.

786
00:53:57,730 --> 00:54:01,540
Boy, girl... you are a sword,

787
00:54:01,740 --> 00:54:02,990
that is all.

788
00:54:04,620 --> 00:54:06,210
That is the grip.

789
00:54:06,990 --> 00:54:09,200
You are not holding a battle-axe.

790
00:54:09,200 --> 00:54:11,320
- You are holding... - A needle.

791
00:54:14,640 --> 00:54:15,830
Just so.

792
00:54:16,650 --> 00:54:18,990
Now we will begin the dance.

793
00:54:19,240 --> 00:54:20,780
Remember, child,

794
00:54:21,560 --> 00:54:24,340
this is not the dance of the Westeros we are learning...

795
00:54:24,390 --> 00:54:25,810
the knight's dance,

796
00:54:25,810 --> 00:54:27,880
hacking and hammering.

797
00:54:28,130 --> 00:54:32,100
This is the bravo's dance...

798
00:54:33,100 --> 00:54:34,960
the water dance.

799
00:54:34,960 --> 00:54:36,450
It is swift

800
00:54:37,410 --> 00:54:38,560
and sudden.

801
00:54:41,200 --> 00:54:43,120
All men are made of water,

802
00:54:43,330 --> 00:54:44,750
do you know this?

803
00:54:45,710 --> 00:54:47,460
If you pierce them,

